---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/docs.astro";
---

<DocsLayout title="Privacy Policy — Querial">
    <div class="space-y-8">
        <div>
            <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-1">Last updated: August 2026</p>
        </div>
        <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 [&>p]:text-muted-foreground [&>h2]:text-foreground">
            <h2>1. Overview</h2>
            <p>
                Querial is a self-hosted control plane. This marketing site does not
                operate your instance, store your pipeline SQL, or receive target database
                credentials. Use of a Querial instance is also subject to the
                <a href="/docs/eula" class="text-link hover:underline">Terms of Use</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>2. What an instance stores</h2>
            <p>
                The organization that runs Querial stores, in its own control database
                (PostgreSQL 18 with pgvector):
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
                <li>Identity accounts, team and project memberships, invites, and preferences (theme, culture, timezone)</li>
                <li>Pipeline designs, published versions, deployments, schedules, runs, logs, and audit snapshots</li>
                <li>Encrypted connection endpoints (AES-256-GCM). APIs never return decrypted secrets</li>
                <li>Hashed API keys (shown in full only at creation)</li>
                <li>Optional SqlAssist embeddings and chat history</li>
                <li>Artifact metadata; object bytes on local disk or an S3-compatible store the operator configures</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Target databases hold business rows and target-local migration history.
                Querial does not copy those rows into the control plane as a warehouse.
            </p>

            <h2>3. What this website stores</h2>
            <p>
                This documentation site is static. Theme preference may be saved in
                browser localStorage (<code class="text-foreground">theme</code>). No
                account is created here. No analytics vendor is required by the site
                template.
            </p>
            <p>
                If you use the
                <a href="/feedback" class="text-link hover:underline">feedback form</a>,
                name, email, subject, and message are sent through Web3Forms so we can
                reply. A captcha may run as part of that provider's spam protection.
                Do not put connection strings, passwords, or other secrets in a
                feedback message.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Optional providers inside an instance</h2>
            <p>
                If an operator enables a cloud LLM for SqlAssist, prompts leave the
                instance only under that operator's configuration. Assistance is
                draft-only. Git remotes, if configured, receive package trees that must
                not contain secrets. Mail for invites uses the operator's SMTP; invite
                send fails closed if mail cannot be sent.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Isolation</h2>
            <p>
                Catalog lists and gets are scoped to the current project. A foreign id
                is not-found. API keys cannot act outside their project. Forged team or
                project cookies are ignored.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
